      "writtenOn": "2024-01-30T19:14:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am with you that using a hash does seem a bit overkill given how few unique load from MSAA pipelines we anticipate seeing.\n\nThat being said, the graphics pipeline key is currently set up w/ some graphics pipeline information first (render step ID, paintParamsID, and write swizzle). \n\nTo iterate and compare keys, we\u0027d have to do one of two things:\n\n1) Call makeGraphicsPipelineKey(...) to get a key for the desired load MSAA pipeline we want to search for. That requires passing in a `GraphicsPipelineDesc`, which we do not have access to from `VulkanCommandBuffer::beginRenderPass` (where we currently deduce whether we need to load MSAA from resolve). \n\nWe could create a mock GraphicsPipelineDesc to represent load msaa pipelines I suppose.\n \n`makeGraphicsPipelineKey` also returns a `UniqueKey` whereas `VulkanGraphicsPipeline`, which extends `Resource`, returns a `GraphiteResourceKey` from its `key()` method. So there\u0027s another inconvenience there.\n\n2) Manually compare just the renderpass components of the entire graphicspipelinekey, requiring a shift of `kUint32sNeededForPipelineInfo` for key comparison.\n\nLMK your thoughts!",
